# Per-deploy state file persistence (T2-01 G-F3). Each fabrik apply writes
# .fabrik/state/<id>.json; destroys move them to _destroyed/. Local audit
# trail only — never committed.
/.fabrik/state/

# Review bundles (T3-03 G-D3). `fabrik review` writes diff + spec + preplan +
# resolved registrars into .fabrik/review/<ts>.md. Local artefact; PR diff
# already captures the change set — never committed.
/.fabrik/review/

# Local artifacts (originally appended by a `fabrik scaffold update` run in the hub)
#
# IMPORTANT — this is /opt/fabrik, the HUB. Fabrik-synced SOURCE files are
# CANONICAL here and MUST stay tracked: .windsurf/, .windsurfrules, CLAUDE.md,
# AGENTS.md, AGENTS-compact.md, opencode.json, scripts/run*, and
# docs/reference/long-command-monitoring.md. They are ignored only in downstream
# *projects* (via the synced block generated by fabrik_synced_manifest.py).
# Do NOT re-add those source files here — only genuine local artifacts belong below.
*.code-workspace
*.db
*.log
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.tmp
*.token
.droid/.kilo_cache_last_refresh
.droid/docs_log/
.droid/docs_queue/
.droid/kilo_models_cache.json
.droid/kilo_usage.jsonl
.droid/reviews/
.droid/traycer-reports/*.md
.env.backup
.env.sysadmin
.modal.toml
.factory/consultations/
/tmp/
Audio_downloads/
Logs/
YT_audio_text/
backups/
cookies*.txt
db/migrations/*.sql
docs/reference/*Search*.md
exports/
pipeline_output/
retry_queue.json
state.json

# Sessional safety backups — files created before destructive edits
# (e.g. `cp AGENTS.md AGENTS.md.backup.YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS`). Kept on disk for
# the duration of the session, never committed to remote history.
*.backup.*
*.bak.*

# Derived kilo pipeline cache — regenerated every run, never source
scripts/kilo-benchmarks/cache/
# Persistent microbench_coding run cache — completions samples survive process
# exit so downstream sanitize/eval failures are $0-recoverable
scripts/kilo-benchmarks/.microbench_cache/
external-services-dashboard.html
# Derived kilo artifacts — regenerated every daily_refresh run, read from disk (not git),
# so tracking them only poisoned the tree (untracked 2026-07-19). translation_bench/cache
# is the per-(model,sentence,lang) API-response cache (bake.py cache_save); models_browser.html
# is the generated single-file viewer (source is models_browser_template.html). kilo_agents.db
# is already covered by *.db above — force-tracked copy removed via git rm --cached; the 13MB
# analytics store is backed up in backups/ and rebuilt by daily_refresh.sh.
scripts/kilo-benchmarks/translation_bench/cache/
scripts/kilo-benchmarks/models_browser.html
# LiveCodeBench grading tool — vendored external (git-clone + sibling venv, grading-only deps),
# never source (coding-benchmark plan 2026-07-19). Rebuilt by the Phase-A provisioning step.
scripts/kilo-benchmarks/.lcb-venv/
scripts/kilo-benchmarks/.lcb-src/
# The LCB HF cache lives at ~/.cache/fabrik/lcb-hf-cache (D-110); this line stays so a re-created copy can never
# ride wip_backup.sh's `add -A` off-box — tests/test_no_orphan_lcb_cache.py is what makes it visible.
scripts/kilo-benchmarks/.lcb-hf-cache/
# Derived kilo selection/route dumps — regenerated every daily_refresh / kilo-review run
# (pre_filter.py, embedding_*.py, category_*.py, kilo_model_sync.py write these from agents.db),
# read from disk not git; tracking them churned the tree with daily +50/-50 reorderings and the
# chore(pipeline) bot re-committed them every day. Untracked 2026-07-26 (same rationale as
# models_browser.html / translation_bench above). Rebuilt on every run — never source.
scripts/kilo_all_models.json
scripts/kilo_47_agents_final.json
scripts/kilo_embeddings_final.json
scripts/kilo_openrouter_routes_final.json
scripts/kilo-benchmarks/embedding_assignments.json
scripts/kilo-benchmarks/openrouter_routes.json
scripts/kilo-benchmarks/shortlists.json

# Tool scratch — regenerable, never committed.
# mutmut's mutation-testing copy of src/+tests/ (185MB); its COPIES of driver
# files also kept tripping the secrets gate with the originals' localhost URLs.
mutants/
# Serena MCP per-project config (tool-local)
.serena/
# Per-repo MCP config (emitted by scripts/sysadmin/emit_mcp_project_config.py; carries resolved DATABASE_URL)
.mcp.json

# Duplicate-detection reports — TOOL OUTPUT, never source. check_duplicates.py's default
# writes duplicate-report.json (+ a sibling jscpd-report.json) into the repo root; the push
# gate was fixed to redirect to /tmp (enforced by tests/test_push_gate_config.py), but these
# two stayed TRACKED from before that fix and churn on every run. Ignored 2026-08-30.
/duplicate-report.json
/jscpd-report.json
/.fabrik/plan-locks/*-salvage-*.diff
.ruff_cache/
/nohup.out

# The usage store's lock file — `claude_p_cost.merge_usage_store` flocks this to serialise the whole
# read-modify-write, because the 06:00 cron and a hand-run `--refresh` are two processes that would
# otherwise lose each other's updates. Pure runtime state: zero bytes, recreated on every merge, and
# meaningless to any other checkout.
/scripts/claude_usage_daily.json.lock
